course: dictionary
lesson: 4996
title: Indoor and outdoor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Indoor is an describing word. It tells you where something happens, is used or is found: inside a building, not outside. Look at the word's parts: in plus door. Inside the door means inside the building.
explain: «Christmas and fairy lights are checked for damage, switched off at night, and indoor lights are never used outdoors.» Indoor lights are made for use inside. The sentence warns you not to use them outside, because outdoor is the opposite of indoor.
explain: «A good home gives a kitten ... indoor life until it is vaccinated and old enough.» Indoor life means the kitten lives inside, away from outside dangers, until it is ready. To check your meaning, swap in inside and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Indoor means happening, used or found inside a building, not outside.
fact: Indoor is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in indoor games, indoor plants and indoor shoes.
fact: The opposite of indoor is outdoor.
fact: Indoor sports and indoor play are often chosen when it is cold or raining.
fact: Look at the parts of a word to help you: indoor is in plus door, so it means inside the door.
exercise: «Indoor games» are played where? | *Inside a building | On the roof of a bus | Outside in the park | In the sea
exercise: Which word means the opposite of indoor? | *Outdoor | Cold | Happy | Indoor plant
exercise: In «indoor lights are never used outdoors», what does indoor describe? | Very bright lights | *Lights made for use inside a building | Lights in the sky | Lights that are always on
test: Which one is an indoor activity? | *Playing table tennis in the sports hall | Flying a kite on a windy hill | Building a sandcastle at the beach
test: Dad says, «Put your indoor shoes on.» What does indoor tell you? | *The shoes are worn inside the house | The shoes are for running in the rain | The shoes are made of wood
exam: «A kitten needs indoor life until it is vaccinated.» What does indoor life mean? | Living only at the vet's | Living in a tree | Living outside in the garden | *Living inside, away from outside dangers, until it is ready
